title op3: a directory rename carries its subtree

# Section 16, the mild half of the parked directory-subtree gap.
#
# Off-of renames /d to /e with rename(2), so the directory keeps its
# dnode and every file underneath keeps both its dnode and its leaf.
# Onto is quiet, so nothing conflicts and the fixture is entirely
# about how the change is READ and what it compiles to.
#
# Under full-path naming three names changed: /d, /d/f and /d/g.
# Both emission compilers therefore emitted three renames, and two of
# them were edits that rename(2) had already performed.  That was a
# real shared bug, found by cross-checking the two compilers against
# each other and fixed in neither, because the fix was not writable
# in full-path coordinates -- see op3-carried-child-rename.
#
# Under the relativized reading (Definition 16.1) the pair
# (base /d, off-of /e) is corresponded by red, and inside that pair
# the leaves f and g are equal on both sides.  Relative to the pair
# the children did not change their names at all.  One name changed,
# not three, and the descendants compile to NO edit (Remark 16.5).
#
# Hand-worked: clean, and the decided tree is base's with the
# directory renamed.  The decision was never in doubt here; what
# changes is the edit list, which the gold section cannot see.  That
# is worth stating rather than hiding: this fixture passes today and
# will pass after the rework, and it is the EDIT COUNT that has to
# be watched.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: d/
      3-100: f = fv0
      4-100: g = gv0

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: d/
      3-100: f = fv0
      4-100: g = gv0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: e/
      3-100: f = fv0
      4-100: g = gv0

#
# WORKED OUTCOME (by hand, before any implementation ran)
#   believed moves:  none needed.  (base /d, off-of /e) is
#                    corresponded by RED, and belief exists only for
#                    the case red cannot see
#   deltas:          none.  Relative to the pair f and g keep their
#                    leaves, so no pool has a lost or gained set
#   decisions:       the directory renames d to e; f and g keep, and
#                    every dnode is reused
#   conflicts:       none, onto is quiet
#   emission:        ONE rename, of the directory, in the root's
#                    scope.  The descendants compile to no edit at
#                    all (Remark 16.5) -- under full-path coordinates
#                    both compilers emitted two more
# --- expected result, worked by hand 2026-08-31 ---
expect clean

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: e
      3-100: f = fv0
      4-100: g = gv0
